IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa14-nouns.l4: the nouns of coa14 (Companies Act 2006, ss 610 to 657): DECLARE and nothing else.
-- No rule, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT. Every type, constructor and field name begins with the label of the provision it
-- serves (the keel's naming rule: a name defined in two modules cannot be used at all, fields and constructors included).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Every quote line below
-- is generated by srcrefs.py quote and checked by srcrefs.py check.
--
-- MEMBERSHIP TEST (from the encoding-a-subject skill): could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact? Only
-- the facts a person can state are fields here. Whether a company IS a subsidiary, a public company, a quoted company is
-- a rule and is asked as a seam input (PLAN.md section 4), never declared here.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 7: SHARE PREMIUMS (ss 610-616)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:8210 | (2) Where, on issuing shares, a company has transferred a sum to the share premium account, it may use that sum to write off—
-- src:8211 | (a) the expenses of the issue of those shares;
-- src:8212 | (b) any commission paid on the issue of those shares.
@ref s 610(2) Application of share premiums: what the sum in the share premium account may be used to write off (src:8210-8212)
DECLARE `s 610(2) use of the sum in the share premium account` IS ONE OF
    `s 610(2)(a) writing off the expenses of the issue of those shares`
    `s 610(2)(b) writing off any commission paid on the issue of those shares`
    `s 610(2) some other use of the sum`

-- src:8248 | (2) Company A has secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B if in consequence of an acquisition or cancellation of equity shares in company B (in pursuance of that arrangement) it holds equity shares in company B of an aggregate amount equal to 90% or more of the nominal value of that company's equity share capital.
-- src:8249 | (3) For this purpose—
-- src:8250 | (a) it is immaterial whether any of those shares were acquired in pursuance of the arrangement; and
-- src:8251 | (b) shares in company B held by the company as treasury shares are excluded in determining the nominal value of company B's share capital.
-- src:8252 | (4) Where the equity share capital of company B is divided into different classes of shares, company A is not regarded as having secured at least a 90% equity holding in company B unless the requirements of subsection (2) are met in relation to each of those classes of shares taken separately.
-- src:8253 | (5) For the purposes of this section shares held by—
-- src:8254 | (a) a company that is company A's holding company or subsidiary, or
-- src:8255 | (b) a subsidiary of company A's holding company, or
-- src:8256 | (c) its or their nominees,
-- src:8257 | are treated as held by company A.
@ref s 613(2) to (5) Merger relief: meaning of 90% equity holding: the facts about one class of company B's equity shares (src:8248-8257)
DECLARE `s 613(2) class of company B's equity share capital` HAS
    `s 613(2) nominal value of the equity shares of the class that company A holds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 613(5)(a) nominal value of the class held by a company that is company A's holding company or subsidiary` IS A NUMBER
    `s 613(5)(b) nominal value of the class held by a subsidiary of company A's holding company` IS A NUMBER
    `s 613(5)(c) nominal value of the class held by the nominees of those companies` IS A NUMBER
    `s 613(2) nominal value of the class in company B's equity share capital, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
    `s 613(3)(b) nominal value of the class held by company B as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER

-- src:8274 | (2) References in this Chapter (however expressed) to—
-- src:8275 | (a) the acquisition by a company of shares in another company, and
-- src:8276 | (b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company,
@ref s 616(2) Interpretation of this Chapter: the acts the subsection extends to a nominee (src:8274-8276)
DECLARE `s 616(2) kind of act` IS ONE OF
    `s 616(2)(a) the acquisition by a company of shares in another company`
    `s 616(2)(b) the issue or allotment of shares to, or the transfer of shares to or by, a company`
    `s 616(2) some other act`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 8: ALTERATION OF SHARE CAPITAL (ss 617-628)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:8284 | (2) The company may—
-- src:8285 | (a) increase its share capital by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part, or
-- src:8286 | (b) reduce its share capital in accordance with Chapter 10.
-- src:8287 | (3) The company may—
-- src:8288 | (a) sub-divide or consolidate all or any of its share capital in accordance with section 618, or
-- src:8289 | (b) reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620.
-- src:8290 | (4) The company may redenominate all or any of its shares in accordance with section 622, and may reduce its share capital in accordance with section 626 in connection with such a redenomination.
-- src:8291 | (5) Nothing in this section affects—
-- src:8292 | (a) the power of a company to purchase its own shares, or to redeem shares, in accordance with Part 18;
-- src:8293 | (b) the power of a company to purchase its own shares in pursuance of an order of the court under—
-- src:8294 | (i) section 98 (application to court to cancel resolution for re-registration as a private company),
-- src:8295 | (ii) section 721(6) (powers of court on objection to redemption or purchase of shares out of capital),
-- src:8296 | (iii) section 759 (remedial order in case of breach of prohibition of public offers by private company), or
-- src:8297 | (iv) Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice);
-- src:8298 | (c) the forfeiture of shares, or the acceptance of shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the company's articles, for failure to pay any sum payable in respect of the shares;
-- src:8299 | (d) the cancellation of shares under section 662 (duty to cancel shares held by or for a public company);
-- src:8300 | (e) the power of a company—
-- src:8301 | (i) to enter into a compromise or arrangement in accordance with Part 26 or 26A (arrangements and reconstructions), or
-- src:8302 | (ii) to do anything required to comply with an order of the court on an application under that Part.
-- src:8303 | (f) the cancellation of a share warrant issued by the company and of the shares specified in it by a cancellation order or suspended cancellation order made under paragraph 6 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015 (cancellation where share warrants not surrendered in accordance with that Schedule);
-- src:8304 | (g) the cancellation of a share warrant issued by the company and of the shares specified in it pursuant to section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2) (cancellation of share warrants on restoration of a company).
@ref s 617(2) to (5) Alteration of share capital of limited company: the ways (src:8284-8304)
DECLARE `s 617 way of altering share capital` IS ONE OF
    `s 617(2)(a) increase the share capital by allotting new shares in accordance with this Part`
    `s 617(2)(b) reduce the share capital in accordance with Chapter 10`
    `s 617(3)(a) sub-divide or consolidate the share capital in accordance with section 618`
    `s 617(3)(b) reconvert stock into shares in accordance with section 620`
    `s 617(4)(a) redenominate shares in accordance with section 622`
    `s 617(4)(b) reduce the share capital in accordance with section 626 in connection with a redenomination`
    `s 617(5)(a) purchase or redeem shares in accordance with Part 18`
    `s 617(5)(b) purchase shares in pursuance of an order of the court under section 98, 721(6), 759 or Part 30`
    `s 617(5)(c) forfeit shares, or accept shares surrendered in lieu, in pursuance of the articles`
    `s 617(5)(d) cancel shares under section 662`
    `s 617(5)(e) compromise or arrangement under Part 26 or 26A, or compliance with a court order on an application under that Part`
    `s 617(5)(f) cancel a share warrant and its shares under paragraph 6 of Schedule 4 to the Small Business, Enterprise and Employment Act 2015`
    `s 617(5)(g) cancel a share warrant and its shares under section 1028A(2) or 1032A(2)`
    `s 617 some other way of altering share capital`

DECLARE `s 617(1) alteration of share capital` HAS
    `s 617 the way the share capital is altered` IS A `s 617 way of altering share capital`
    `s 617 the alteration is made in accordance with the provision that names the way` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8307 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may—
-- src:8308 | (a) sub-divide its shares, or any of them, into shares of a smaller nominal amount than its existing shares, or
-- src:8309 | (b) consolidate and divide all or any of its share capital into shares of a larger nominal amount than its existing shares.
@ref s 618(1) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: the two powers (src:8307-8309)
DECLARE `s 618(1) kind of change to shares` IS ONE OF
    `s 618(1)(a) sub-division into shares of a smaller nominal amount`
    `s 618(1)(b) consolidation and division into shares of a larger nominal amount`

-- src:8312 | (4) A resolution under subsection (3) may authorise a company—
-- src:8313 | (a) to exercise more than one of the powers conferred by this section;
-- src:8314 | (b) to exercise a power on more than one occasion;
-- src:8315 | (c) to exercise a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances.
@ref s 618(4) Sub-division or consolidation of shares: what a resolution may authorise (src:8312-8315)
DECLARE `s 618(4) what the resolution authorises` IS ONE OF
    `s 618(4)(a) the exercise of more than one of the powers`
    `s 618(4)(b) the exercise of a power on more than one occasion`
    `s 618(4)(c) the exercise of a power at a specified time or in specified circumstances`
    `s 618(4) something else`

-- src:8337 | (3) A resolution under subsection (2) may authorise a company to exercise the power conferred by this section—
-- src:8338 | (a) on more than one occasion;
-- src:8339 | (b) at a specified time or in specified circumstances.
@ref s 620(3) Reconversion of stock into shares: what a resolution may authorise (src:8337-8339)
DECLARE `s 620(3) what the resolution authorises` IS ONE OF
    `s 620(3)(a) the exercise of the power on more than one occasion`
    `s 620(3)(b) the exercise of the power at a specified time or in specified circumstances`
    `s 620(3) something else`

-- src:8324 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:8325 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:8326 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:8327 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
@ref s 619(3) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: what the statement of capital must state (one class entry) (src:8324-8327)
DECLARE `s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital` HAS
    `s 619(3)(c)(i) states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 619(3)(c)(ii) states the total number of shares of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 619(3)(c)(iii) states the aggregate nominal value of the shares of the class` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8320 | (3) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital immediately following the exercise of the power—
-- src:8321 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:8322 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:8323 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
@ref s 619(3) Notice to registrar of sub-division or consolidation: what the statement of capital must state (src:8320-8323)
DECLARE `s 619(3) statement of capital` HAS
    `s 619(3)(a) states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 619(3)(b) states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 619(3)(ba) states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 619(3)(c) the entries for each class of shares` IS A LIST OF `s 619(3)(c) class entry in a statement of capital`
    `s 619(3) is stated with respect to the share capital at the moment the section names` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8361 | (3) The rate must be either—
-- src:8362 | (a) a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution, or
-- src:8363 | (b) a rate determined by taking the average of rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution.
@ref s 622(3) Redenomination of share capital: the kinds of rate (src:8361-8363)
DECLARE `s 622(3) kind of rate of exchange` IS ONE OF
    `s 622(3)(a) a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution`
    `s 622(3)(b) the average of the rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution`
    `s 622(3) some other rate`

-- src:8380 | (1) The redenomination of shares does not affect any rights or obligations of members under the company's constitution, or any restrictions affecting members under the company's constitution.
-- src:8381 | In particular, it does not affect entitlement to dividends (including entitlement to dividends in a particular currency), voting rights or any liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares.
@ref s 624(1) Effect of redenomination: the matters it does not affect (src:8380-8381)
DECLARE `s 624(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 624(1) a right or obligation of a member under the company's constitution`
    `s 624(1) a restriction affecting a member under the company's constitution`
    `s 624(1) entitlement to dividends`
    `s 624(1) entitlement to dividends in a particular currency`
    `s 624(1) voting rights`
    `s 624(1) liability in respect of amounts unpaid on shares`
    `s 624(1) some other matter`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 9: CLASSES OF SHARE AND CLASS RIGHTS (ss 629-640)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:8466 | Nothing in section 630 or 631 (variation of class rights) affects the power of the court under—
-- src:8467 | section 98 (application to cancel resolution for public company to be re-registered as private),
-- src:8468 | Part 26 (arrangements and reconstructions: general)
-- src:8469 | Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty), or
-- src:8470 | Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice).
@ref s 632 Variation of class rights: saving for court's powers under other provisions (src:8466-8470)
DECLARE `s 632 power of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 632 the power of the court under section 98`
    `s 632 the power of the court under Part 26`
    `s 632 the power of the court under Part 26A`
    `s 632 the power of the court under Part 30`
    `s 632 some other power of the court`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- CHAPTER 10: REDUCTION OF SHARE CAPITAL (ss 641-653)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:8530 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may reduce its share capital—
-- src:8531 | (a) in the case of a private company limited by shares, by special resolution supported by a solvency statement (see sections 642 to 644);
-- src:8532 | (b) in any case, by special resolution confirmed by the court (see sections 645 to 651).
@ref s 641(1) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: the two routes (src:8530-8532)
DECLARE `s 641(1) route of reduction` IS ONE OF
    `s 641(1)(a) special resolution supported by a solvency statement`
    `s 641(1)(b) special resolution confirmed by the court`

-- src:8543 | (4) In particular, a company may—
-- src:8544 | (a) extinguish or reduce the liability on any of its shares in respect of share capital not paid up, or
-- src:8545 | (b) either with or without extinguishing or reducing liability on any of its shares—
-- src:8546 | (i) cancel any paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets, or
-- src:8547 | (ii) repay any paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants.
@ref s 641(4) Circumstances in which a company may reduce its share capital: the particular kinds of reduction (src:8543-8547)
DECLARE `s 641(4) kind of reduction` IS ONE OF
    `s 641(4)(a) extinguishing or reducing the liability on shares in respect of share capital not paid up`
    `s 641(4)(b)(i) cancelling paid-up share capital that is lost or unrepresented by available assets`
    `s 641(4)(b)(ii) repaying paid-up share capital in excess of the company's wants`
    `s 641(4) some other kind of reduction`

-- src:8560 | (1) A solvency statement is a statement that each of the directors—
-- src:8561 | (a) has formed the opinion, as regards the company's situation at the date of the statement, that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts; and
-- src:8562 | (b) has also formed the opinion—
-- src:8563 | (i) if it is intended to commence the winding up of the company within twelve months of that date, that the company will be able to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts in full within twelve months of the commencement of the winding up; or
-- src:8564 | (ii) in any other case, that the company will be able to pay (or otherwise discharge) its debts as they fall due during the year immediately following that date.
@ref s 643(1) Solvency statement: what each director must have formed an opinion on (src:8560-8564)
DECLARE `s 643(1) director's opinions` HAS
    `s 643(1)(a) has formed the opinion that there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 643(1)(b)(i) has formed the opinion that the company will pay its debts in full within twelve months of the commencement of the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 643(1)(b)(ii) has formed the opinion that the company will pay its debts as they fall due during the year immediately following the date` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8638 | (2) The court must not confirm the reduction unless it is satisfied, with respect to every creditor of the company who is entitled to object to the reduction of capital that either—
-- src:8639 | (a) his consent to the reduction has been obtained, or
-- src:8640 | (b) his debt or claim has been discharged, or has determined or has been secured.
@ref s 648(2) Court order confirming reduction: the creditors the court must be satisfied about (src:8638-8640)
DECLARE `s 648(2) creditor entitled to object` HAS
    `s 648(2)(a) the creditor's consent to the reduction has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 648(2)(b) the creditor's debt or claim has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 648(2)(b) the creditor's debt or claim has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 648(2)(b) the creditor's debt or claim has been secured` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8656 | (3) The resolution for reducing share capital, as confirmed by the court's order, takes effect—
-- src:8657 | (a) in the case of a reduction of share capital that forms part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26 (arrangements and reconstructions: general)—
-- src:8658 | (i) on delivery of the order and statement of capital to the registrar, or
-- src:8659 | (ii) if the court so orders, on the registration of the order and statement of capital;
-- src:8660 | (aa) in the case of a reduction of share capital that forms part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned by the court under Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty)—
-- src:8661 | (i) in the case of any company other than one to which sub-paragraph (ii) applies, on delivery of the order and statement of capital to the registrar;
-- src:8662 | (ii) in the case of an overseas company that is not required to register particulars under section 1046, on publication of the order and statement of capital in the Gazette;
-- src:8663 | (iii) in either case, if the court so orders, on the registration of the order and statement of capital;
-- src:8664 | (b) in any case not falling within paragraph (a) or (aa), on the registration of the order and statement of capital.
@ref s 649(3) Registration of order and statement of capital: when the resolution takes effect (src:8656-8664)
DECLARE `s 649(3) kind of reduction for the time it takes effect` IS ONE OF
    `s 649(3)(a) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26`
    `s 649(3)(aa)(i) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, a company other than an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046`
    `s 649(3)(aa)(ii) part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned under Part 26A, an overseas company not required to register particulars under section 1046`
    `s 649(3)(b) any case not within paragraph (a) or (aa)`

-- src:8669 | (b) is conclusive evidence—
-- src:8670 | (i) that the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with, and
-- src:8671 | (ii) that the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital.
@ref s 649(6) Registration of order and statement of capital: what the certificate is conclusive evidence of (src:8669-8671)
DECLARE `s 649(6)(b) matter the certificate is evidence of` IS ONE OF
    `s 649(6)(b)(i) the requirements of this Act with respect to the reduction of share capital have been complied with`
    `s 649(6)(b)(ii) the company's share capital is as stated in the statement of capital`
    `s 649(6)(b) some other matter`
